/// A Wi-Fi network in range, from NetworkManager's last scan; access
/// points of one network name are one entry (the strongest). Keyed by
/// `ssid`.
record AccessPoint key ssid {
  /// The network's name.
  ssid: text
  /// Signal strength, 0 to 1.
  strength: float
  /// It needs a password: a WPA, WPA2 or WPA3 personal or a WEP network,
  /// which `connect_with` joins (a network menu's password field). An
  /// open or Enhanced Open network takes none, and an enterprise
  /// (802.1X) one joins through its saved profile, with `connect()`.
  secure: bool
  /// It is the network joined.
  active: bool
  /// Joins it: with its saved connection if there is one, else a new one
  /// (for a `secure` network NetworkManager asks its secret agent for the
  /// password); an enterprise (802.1X) network with no saved profile is
  /// refused (it is set up in the system's network settings). A failure,
  /// including one NetworkManager reports later (no password, a wrong
  /// one, a timeout), is `network.failed`.
  action connect()
  /// Joins a `secure` network with `password` (its WPA key or WEP key),
  /// saved in its connection: a network menu's password field. On any
  /// other network it fails. A failure is `network.failed`.
  action connect_with(password: text)
}

/// The network, from NetworkManager, followed live.
service network {
  /// A network connection is up.
  connected: bool
  /// The Wi-Fi network joined, if any.
  ssid: text?
  /// The Wi-Fi signal strength, 0 to 1.
  strength: float
  /// The Wi-Fi radio is on. Writable.
  wifi: bool rw
  /// The Wi-Fi networks in range, keyed by `ssid`. Scanned only while a
  /// visible reader reads them (a network menu that is open).
  access_points: [AccessPoint]
  /// Joining a network failed (no password and no secret agent to ask
  /// for one, a wrong one, out of range, timed out): `on
  /// network.failed(ssid, error) { … }`.
  event failed(ssid: text, error: text)
}
